WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.219
Hi, I'm Steve Sickles with Consolidated Label,
here to explain flexographic printing.

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:14.579
To start, flexographic presses are giant printing machines

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:18.320
superb at delivering high-end graphics
at rapid speed and low-cost.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.619
Capable of completing large orders very quickly, 
flexographic presses 

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:25.520
can print onto almost any material
including paper, film and metal foils.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.160
At Consolidated Label, we've expanded the
capabilities of our flexographic presses

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.890
for more complicated processes
such as cold foiling, embossing and silk screening.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.560
Flexographic presses are web-fed,
meaning they are continuously fed materials

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.950
from large rolls of material stock, 
and allows us to print an average

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.240
 of 350 feet per minute.
That's four miles of material an hour!

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.960
Flexography, or "Flexo," is a form of
printing process which utilizes

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.870
a flexible relief plate. Our plates
are thin sheets of polymer material that

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:57.020
have been coated with a photosensitive surface.
The relief image is a positive mirrored,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.650
laser-engraved printing plate of digital artwork,
which is wrapped around a print cylinder,

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:04.199
and installed into the press. 
The plate transfers the ink, and prints

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:07.820
onto the passing web material. Each desired color
within the label requires its own

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.250
individual plate. And with 10 ink stations,
we are capable of up to 10 colors

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.100
with every flex press run.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.800
What does 10 color capability mean?
It's simple:

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.650
Flexo can achieve virtually any color
combination with the four color process

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.439
of Cyan, Magenta, Yellow
and Black colored inks.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:26.079
but some artworks may demand more than
one shade of any given color. Such as

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:29.970
mixes of Magenta being used for pink, 
maroon, and crimson on a single project.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:33.790
These desired variations require using
matching Pantone colors for a more

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.350
accurate color match. We use a computerized
ink matching system to create these Pantone colors,

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.300
which allow us to print multiple variations
of any certain color.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.080
With 10 ink stations possible, that's 10 different colors,
and there's not much we can't handle.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.810
At Consolidated Label, we use water-based
and ultraviolet curable inks, which do not

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.850
dry in the air, and create sharp colors
using less ink.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:56.819
these differ from solvent inks, which
are often found in personal, inkjet printers

00:01:56.819 --> 00:01:58.430
and are harmful to the environment.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.430
After the UV ink is printed onto the
material, the web travels through

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.280
a UV lamp, which cures the ink.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.880
In other words, it turns the liquid
ink into solid matter.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.880
These inks reduce our setup time,
as they come press-ready, 

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.179
lowering our production costs.

00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:12.729
After the label has been printed,
the last stop on the flexo press

00:02:12.729 --> 00:02:14.120
is the cutting die.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.550
A cutting die is a cylindrical blade
that shapes the label by cutting off all the

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.450
excess material. Each die is custom ordered
to match the label specifications

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.050
made by the customer.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.620
At Consolidated Label, we utilize
an entire fleet of flexographic presses

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.350
to readily serve thousands of
customers, nationwide, with

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.269
high-quality product labels.

00:02:31.269 --> 00:02:34.709
I hope this video has been helpful
in understanding flexographic printing.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:37.849
Should you be requiring labels for
either long, or short run,

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:40.150
please contact our 
Customer Service department.

